IMPORT prelude

-- State Lands Act 1920 (Singapore) -- what a State title holder actually lives with: how deep the land goes (s 9), the conditions
-- implied into grants and leases by date of issue (s 11(2) to (5)), the grantee's implied covenants and when breach lets the
-- Collector re-enter (ss 13, 14(1)(e), 14(2)), the State's mineral royalty and right to take materials (s 14(1)(a), (b)), notice
-- not needed to bind a successor (s 15), the 50% cap on rent revision (s 16(2), (3)), forfeiture of religious or charitable land
-- (s 17(1)), and the boundary duty with its double-cost recovery (s 29).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SLA1920.txt, incorporating
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 (latest annotated amending Act seen in the body: 11/2015).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rights and burdens that run with a
-- State title. Not encoded: the Chief Valuer and the Commissioner of Lands (ss 3 to 6), rule-making (ss 7, 16(5) to (7), 27), modes
-- of alienation (s 8), the subjacent-support easement (s 10), the deceased grantee (s 12), Collector's Certificates and survey
-- (ss 18, 19), surrender and regrant (ss 20, 21, 23, 24), grants in fee simple to HDB and of road reserves (ss 22, 25, 26), the
-- treaty vesting power (s 17(2)) and where fees are paid (s 28).
--
-- Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `State Lands Act 1920 -- grants and leases`

§§ `9 -- how far down the land goes`

-- s 9(1): "any land includes only so much of the subterranean space as is reasonably necessary for the use and enjoyment of the
-- land, being -- (a) the depth of subterranean space that is specified in the State title for that land; or (b) if no such depth is
-- specified, subterranean space to -30.000 metres from the Singapore Height Datum." s 9(3) reads the same default into references
-- in other written law.
-- Depths are written here as metres BELOW the Singapore Height Datum (30 for -30.000 m). That a stratum exactly at the limit is
-- included ("to") is an inference.
GIVEN `the title specifies a depth` IS A BOOLEAN, `the specified depth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the depth of the land below the Datum` MEANS
    IF `the title specifies a depth` THEN `the specified depth` ELSE 30

GIVEN `the title specifies a depth` IS A BOOLEAN, `the specified depth` IS A NUMBER, `the stratum depth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stratum is part of the land` IF
    `the stratum depth` AT MOST `the depth of the land below the Datum` `the title specifies a depth` `the specified depth`

§§ `11(2) to (5) -- conditions implied by date of issue`

-- s 11(2): in every grant and every lease made "after 3 May 1907" there is implied, "in the absence of an express provision to the
-- contrary", a reservation to the State of the right "to enter upon the land and to search for and take any mineral oil", paying
-- compensation for damage as assessed by the Collector.
GIVEN `the issue date` IS A NUMBER, `the instrument expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mineral oil reservation is implied` IF
    `the issue date` GREATER THAN 19070503 AND (NOT `the instrument expressly provides otherwise`)

-- s 11(3): if the person is dissatisfied with the Collector's assessment "the difference ... must be referred to arbitration", and
-- "the sending in by that person of a claim to compensation after the Collector has made an offer of compensation in writing must be
-- treated as a submission to arbitration under the Arbitration Act 2001".
GIVEN `the Collector made a written offer` IS A BOOLEAN, `a claim was sent in after the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is treated as a submission to arbitration` IF
    `the Collector made a written offer` AND `a claim was sent in after the offer`

-- s 11(4): in every grant or lease made "after 1 December 1915" there is implied, absent express contrary provision, that an
-- adjacent owner or occupier may claim from the Collector a right of way to the nearest public road; the Collector may mark out a
-- way; the claimant may pass over it "making full compensation for damage done to growing crops and permanent improvements" and
-- bears the cost of making and maintaining it; disputes are settled by the Collector "whose decision is final".
GIVEN `the issue date` IS A NUMBER, `the instrument expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the right-of-way condition is implied` IF
    `the issue date` GREATER THAN 19151201 AND (NOT `the instrument expressly provides otherwise`)

-- s 11(5): "Every grant of land issued under subsection (1) before 1 March 1961 is deemed to confer an estate in perpetuity on the
-- grantee."
GIVEN `the issue date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant is deemed an estate in perpetuity` IF
    `the issue date` LESS THAN 19610301

§§ `13 and 14(1)(e), 14(2) -- the grantee's covenants and re-entry`

-- s 13(1): implied in every grant, absent express contrary provision, covenants by the grantee (a) to pay the rent; (b) to "maintain
-- in substantial repair all landmarks"; (c) not to use any portion "for the burial of a human body without the Minister's written
-- permission"; (d) not to "assign or demise the land in parcels or otherwise than the entirety thereof except in the case of a lease
-- for a term not exceeding 7 years". (2) the burden runs with the land.
GIVEN `deals with only part of the land` IS A BOOLEAN, `the dealing is a lease` IS A BOOLEAN, `the lease term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing breaches the entirety covenant` IF
    `deals with only part of the land` AND (NOT (`the dealing is a lease` AND `the lease term in years` AT MOST 7))

-- s 13(3): if the grantee assigns and "the assignment is duly registered", the grantee's personal liability for "future rent which
-- becomes due under the grant after the date of such registration ceases as from that date".
GIVEN `the grantee has assigned the land` IS A BOOLEAN, `the assignment is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the rent fell due after registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the original grantee is personally liable for the rent` IF
    NOT (`the grantee has assigned the land` AND `the assignment is registered` AND `the rent fell due after registration`)

-- s 14(1)(e): for breach of "any of the implied covenants mentioned in section 13 OTHER THAN those for the payment of rent and the
-- maintenance of landmarks", the Collector may re-enter "on any portion of the land in the name of the whole" and the land "is
-- forfeited to and vests in the Government".
-- s 14(2): for grants and leases "issued after 1 January 1936", (a) no opening, working or digging for oil, mines, minerals,
-- quarries, laterite, clay, gravel or sand without the President's written consent, "except materials for the making of or repairing
-- new or existing roads on the land"; (b) breach carries the same re-entry and forfeiture.
DECLARE Breach IS ONE OF
    `non-payment of rent`
    `failing to maintain the boundary landmarks`
    `burial without the Minister's written permission`
    `dealing with part of the land`
    `digging for minerals without consent`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach, `the issue date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Collector may re-enter and forfeit` IF
    CONSIDER `the breach`
    WHEN `non-payment of rent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `failing to maintain the boundary landmarks` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `burial without the Minister's written permission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `dealing with part of the land` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `the issue date` GREATER THAN 19360101

GIVEN `the issue date` IS A NUMBER, `the President consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `the material is for roads on the land` IS A BOOLEAN, `the instrument expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the digging breaches the mining condition` IF
        `the issue date` GREATER THAN 19360101
    AND (NOT `the President consented in writing`)
    AND (NOT `the material is for roads on the land`)
    AND (NOT `the instrument expressly provides otherwise`)

§§ `14(1)(a), (b) -- the State's royalty and materials`

-- s 14(1)(a): "there is reserved to the State a royalty of 10% of the gross produce of all mines and minerals other than laterite".
GIVEN `the gross produce` IS A NUMBER, `the mineral is laterite` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the State's royalty` MEANS
    IF `the mineral is laterite` THEN 0 ELSE `the gross produce` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 14(1)(b): earth, clay, gravel, sand, stone and other materials required for "roads, public buildings or other public purposes"
-- may be taken by the State from the land -- NOT from the site of a dwelling house, a building attached or adjoining it, its
-- "curtilage, garden or orchard", the close in which it is built, or "pleasure grounds adjoining and belonging to" it -- "without
-- compensation except for actual damage done to growing crops, roads, paths, fruit trees or buildings".
DECLARE Spot IS ONE OF
    `open land away from any dwelling house`
    `the site of a dwelling house`
    `a building adjoining a dwelling house`
    `the curtilage, garden or orchard of a dwelling house`
    `pleasure grounds belonging to a dwelling house`

GIVEN `the spot` IS A Spot
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the State may take materials from` IF
    CONSIDER `the spot`
    WHEN `open land away from any dwelling house` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Loss IS ONE OF
    `damage to growing crops`
    `damage to roads`
    `damage to paths`
    `damage to fruit trees`
    `damage to buildings`
    `the value of the materials taken`
    `loss of amenity`

GIVEN `the loss` IS A Loss
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compensation is payable for` IF
    CONSIDER `the loss`
    WHEN `the value of the materials taken` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `loss of amenity` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `15 -- successors bound without notice`

-- s 15(1): an assignee or proprietor "is bound by the exceptions, reservations or covenants (restrictive or otherwise) contained in
-- the Crown grant or lease, or State grant or lease, irrespective of whether the assignee or proprietor has notice (actual or
-- constructive)". (2): applies to all grants and leases issued "before, on or after 15 January 1981".
GIVEN `the proprietor had notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `the issue date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proprietor is bound by the title's covenants` IF
    TRUE

§§ `16(2), (3) -- revision of rent`

-- s 16(2): after 1 January 1915 and at the end of every 30 years the Minister may revise the rent, "but so that the rent payable in
-- any such term of 30 years does not exceed by more than 50% the rent which was payable in the immediately preceding term".
-- (3): "improvements made by the landholder or the landholder's predecessors in title must not be taken into account".
GIVEN `the previous rent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the highest revised rent` MEANS
    `the previous rent` TIMES 150 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `the previous rent` IS A NUMBER, `the revised rent` IS A NUMBER, `improvements were taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent revision is within the Act` IF
    `the revised rent` AT MOST `the highest revised rent` `the previous rent` AND (NOT `improvements were taken into account`)

§§ `17(1) -- religious and charitable land`

-- s 17(1): land granted or leased "free of rent, or at merely nominal rent, as a building site for a religious edifice, or otherwise
-- for religious or charitable purposes, is forfeited to and vests in the Government if at any time the land or the building on the
-- land is applied without the written consent of the President to purposes other than those (if any) specified in the grant or
-- lease". (3): this applies "to all grants and leases whenever made".
GIVEN `granted free or at nominal rent` IS A BOOLEAN, `granted for religious or charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied to another purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the religious or charitable land is forfeited` IF
        `granted free or at nominal rent`
    AND `granted for religious or charitable purposes`
    AND `applied to another purpose`
    AND (NOT `the President consented in writing`)

§§ `29 -- boundaries with State land`

-- s 29(1): every owner or occupier of land abutting State land "must define and keep defined the boundary" by "some wall, bank,
-- drains, fence, road or path, or other sufficient means". (2): in default the Collector may serve written notice. (3): "If the
-- defining or renewal of the boundary is not commenced within 30 days from the date the notice is served and diligently proceeded
-- with, the Collector may cause the boundary to be defined or renewed and recover twice the amount of the cost necessarily
-- incurred ... as if the cost were an arrear of rent".
-- Reading "not commenced within 30 days ... and diligently proceeded with" as: either not begun by day 30, or begun but not
-- diligently pursued (an inference).
GIVEN `a notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since service` IS A NUMBER, `work began within 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN, `work is being diligently pursued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Collector may define the boundary at the owner's cost` IF
        `a notice was served`
    AND (    (`days since service` GREATER THAN 30 AND (NOT `work began within 30 days`))
         OR  (`work began within 30 days` AND (NOT `work is being diligently pursued`)))

GIVEN `the cost necessarily incurred` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount the Collector may recover` MEANS
    `the cost necessarily incurred` TIMES 2
